# Happy Paint — Supabase client configuration (example).
#
# Copy to `.env` (web) / `.env.local` and fill in from your Supabase project:
#   Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API
#     Project URL  -> *_SUPABASE_URL
#     anon public  -> *_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   (PUBLIC — safe to ship in the client;
#                                            RLS is the real security boundary.)
#
# IMPORTANT: when these are UNSET the apps run LOCAL-ONLY — drawing, layers,
# loops, gallery, and the Paint Space locker persist in IndexedDB / on-device
# storage and there is NO account, sync, or social. Set them to turn Supabase on.
#
# Do NOT put the service_role key here or anywhere client-side; it bypasses RLS
# and is only used by the purge-account Edge Function (server-side secret).

# --- Web (Vite static build, hosted on DigitalOcean App Platform) ---
# Vite only exposes vars prefixed with VITE_ and inlines them at BUILD TIME.
# Mirror these into .do/app.yaml (scope BUILD_TIME) for DigitalOcean.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Mobile (Expo / EAS) ---
# Expo only exposes vars prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ to the app bundle.
# Set these in the mobile app env / EAS build secrets (eas.json or EAS dashboard).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
